<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mediterranean</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mediterranean Sea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mediterranean Sea lies between southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. It has been one of the great arenas of trade, migration and warfare throughout history. Empires such as the Punic, Roman, Byzantine, Fatimid and Ottoman empires competed to control its routes, while trans-Saharan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> networks linked it to distant regions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mediterranean.jpg" alt="Mediterranean" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: of the modification : Eric Gaba (Sting) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
